{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/270888-wraith-20th-anniversary-edition-vs-orpheus","id":270888,"title":"Wraith 20th Anniversary Edition vs Orpheus","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-02T10:14:24-07:00","id":270888,"title":"Wraith 20th Anniversary Edition vs Orpheus","content":"I have no clue if this has been cleared up yet, but I was unable to find it anywhere. As far as I can tell, the 20th Anniversary Editions are taking up where the WoD left off. Orpheus, which I believe is Canon, states almost all or all (except for one) wraiths have been destroyed or turned into spectres. It seemed all ghosts were then being generated Orpheus style rather than Wraith. Is this going to be ignored/retcon'ed? Or will this be addressed in the 20th Anniversary Edition? Personally, I liked the ease of use of the Orpheus rules, but classic Wraith had a lot of flavor. Does anyone know if this has been answered? Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3983-kingdavid","name":"KingDavid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T10:28:55-07:00","id":270899,"title":"","content":"Orpheus would be more akin to Geist the Sin Eaters from what I've heard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T10:30:14-07:00","id":270902,"title":"","content":"The impression I got is that basically every line was backing off a little from the apocalypse endgame. It would be neat to see someone compile timelines of &quot;these things happened in W20&quot;, &quot;these ones are questionable&quot; (lots), and &quot;this definitely didn't happen&quot;. Don't know a lot about Wraith myself, but if it's metaplotty, happened near the end of the oWoD, and is getting in the way of your good time, you can probably assume it's not canon anymore at least in your game and expect to see some kind of consensus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T15:27:05-07:00","id":271137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingDavid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/270888-wraith-20th-anniversary-edition-vs-orpheus#post270888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no clue if this has been cleared up yet, but I was unable to find it anywhere. As far as I can tell, the 20th Anniversary Editions are taking up where the WoD left off. Orpheus, which I believe is Canon, states almost all or all (except for one) wraiths have been destroyed or turned into spectres. It seemed all ghosts were then being generated Orpheus style rather than Wraith. Is this going to be ignored/retcon'ed? Or will this be addressed in the 20th Anniversary Edition? Personally, I liked the ease of use of the Orpheus rules, but classic Wraith had a lot of flavor. Does anyone know if this has been answered? Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the x20 lines isn't taking up where OWoD left off as it ended with the Time of Judgement, the apocalyptic end of all the lines. The x20 lines actually step the metaplot back to before the events of the summer of 1999, where we saw the Week of Nightmares, the Sixth Great Maelstrom and the Avatar Storm kick off the beginning of the march to the end. So that means that Wr20 will take place, in terms of metaplot, before the 6GM ravaged the Underworld and ended WtO. Does that mean that Orpheus doesn't or can't exist in that universe, no as the Orpheus Group already existed back then and were conducting their experiments. Whether or not they will appear in some capacity in Wr20 is currently unknown. Dansky has stated that the primary focus of Wr20 is WtO but that doesn't discount the possibility of them getting mentioned in the sections talking about groups among the Quick that interact with the Dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-03T13:03:56-07:00","id":271699,"title":"","content":"The 20th Anniversary Editions are metaplot-agnostic, which is to say that as much of the metaplot is canon as the Storyteller desires. It will not run off the assumption that the Sixth Great Maelstrom has happened any more than V20 assumes that the Week of Nightmares has happened i.e. not at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T10:10:06-07:00","id":272322,"title":"","content":"What I've seen from the two the 20th Anniversary Editions we already have, they <i>sorta</i> pick up right before the end of each line, but not completely, but in a lot of ways, but not really, but... Well, you get the picture. There are odd bits-and-bobs in both <b>V20</b> and <b>W20</b> that hint at, if not outright point at, events that brought about the Time of Judgment, but for the most part, Onyx Path (and old White Wolf in the case of the <b>V20</b> core) decided to keep it 'metaplot agnostic' with a 'year zero' approach. That is, history exists, but they are not going to mandate any things happen that you're expected to put into your chronicles. With <b>Wraith</b>, though, it's gonna be a little odd since <i>Ends of Empire</i> came out well before the rest of the Time of Judgment books did.<br /> <br /> As for <b>Orpheus</b> being considered 'canon' it gets murky. I remember someone telling us that both <b>Orpheus</b> and [d]Demon: the Fallen[/b] were, at best, obliquely 'canon' in the World of Darkness, presumably meaning that those games' internal history and milieus only applied to their own games. Thing is, each of those games leaned on <b>Wraith: the Oblivion</b> in ways that made it nigh-impossible for many of us uncouple from that source material. Further, add in that the Revised Editions of <b>Vampire</b>, <b>Mage</b>, even to a decent extent even <b>Werewolf</b> relied on mechanics and setting elements from <b>Wraith</b> more than any of their previous versions did. However, as we all know, <b>Wraith</b> never received a Revised Edition, making <b>Orpheus</b> the closest we got in that era.<br /> <br /> ...All of the above really just boils down to saying: I dunno how <b>Wraith 20</b> will handle much of anything, but I am proper chuffed that it's getting made! I love that game to bits, and I cannot wait to see how it actually comes together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T21:51:27-07:00","id":272722,"title":"","content":"Yeah; not only does Wr20 not assume that the 6GM has happened, it also doesn\u2019t assume that the 6GM <i>will</i> happen. Personally, I\u2019m hoping that Orpheus makes an appearance in the Wr20 line; but if it does, it will be as a very different thing than its original incarnation: Stygia will still be there when Orpheus starts trying to recruit ghosts, for one thing; and I doubt that the Deathlords will be amused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T12:06:53-07:00","id":273135,"title":"","content":"Well I'd imagine they'd seem them as Dictum Mortuum-violating Renegades. I'm more interesting in how they'd react to the Orpheus Group and their projectors interacting with ghosts and even venturing into the Underworld. Technically they aren't supposed to interfere with the living but what do you do when the living start coming to you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T04:22:51-07:00","id":273601,"title":"","content":"I hope for a &quot;future fate&quot; section in the book, that simply tells us the events from the metaplot and <i><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product_info.php?products_id=123&amp;affiliate_id=171789\" target=\"_blank\">Ends of Empire</a></i> in a shortened version. V20 did the same with sidebars and entries for some clans and bloodlines and I wish M20 would do the same.<br /> I know, that at least one of the revised Convent books stated, that the <i>Time of Judgement</i> has passed and was not the end of the world, but if that was a good thing is arguably. I personally, wish for the 20th Anniversary editions to be timeless, and if the present the world in a certain way, it should be a no-brainer to add a sidebar and tell the reader, that something about this aspect of the world is/was/will be different in books from other editions, due to what ever reason.<br /> I certainly hold a grudge that W20 didn't do this, when it changed rules regarding pre-change-garou-kids and side-stepping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T06:40:07-07:00","id":273732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/270888-wraith-20th-anniversary-edition-vs-orpheus?p=273601#post273601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope for a &quot;future fate&quot; section in the book, that simply tells us the events from the metaplot and <i><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product_info.php?products_id=123&amp;affiliate_id=171789\" target=\"_blank\">Ends of Empire</a></i> in a shortened version. V20 did the same with sidebars and entries for some clans and bloodlines and I wish M20 would do the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, it will. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/270888-wraith-20th-anniversary-edition-vs-orpheus?p=273601#post273601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know, that at least one of the revised Convent books stated, that the <i>Time of Judgement</i> has passed and was not the end of the world, but if that was a good thing is arguably. I personally, wish for the 20th Anniversary editions to be timeless, and if the present the world in a certain way, it should be a no-brainer to add a sidebar and tell the reader, that something about this aspect of the world is/was/will be different in books from other editions, due to what ever reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s worth noting that you\u2019re talking about the <i>Revised Edition\u2019s</i> Convention Books; the 20th Anniversary Edition took some inspiration from them, but is its own thing. And its author has explicitly and repeatedly said that he\u2019ll be making extensive use of \u201cfuture fates\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T07:09:10-07:00","id":273784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/270888-wraith-20th-anniversary-edition-vs-orpheus?p=273732#post273732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s worth noting that you\u2019re talking about the <i>Revised Edition\u2019s</i> Convention Books;</div> </div> </div> </div>Only kindof. I mean, sure they pre-date M20, but they also are 2013 books, not 2003 or 2004. When this books were written/edited/adjusted/finalised the whole Onyx Path license deal was established and it was clear, that V20 and W20 would get additional supplements (V20 already had) and that the cWoD in general would get new material.<br /> So, the &quot;out-of-game&quot; circumstances had changed considerably and this shines though in the books. So, yes, they are nominally (and game mechanically) revised Edition, but practically they don't necessarily fit in the revised Edition that ended with the Time of Judgement - not if they state that the Time of Judgement wasn't the end of the world....<br /> There was a topic about that somewhere, maybe in the forum software before this one, I don't know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/270888-wraith-20th-anniversary-edition-vs-orpheus?p=273732#post273732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And its author has explicitly and repeatedly said that he\u2019ll be making extensive use of \u201cfuture fates\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm glab to read this. Hope it holds true for M20, Wr20, VDA20 and a Changeling20, too.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T09:38:12-07:00","id":273930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/270888-wraith-20th-anniversary-edition-vs-orpheus?p=273601#post273601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know, that at least one of the revised Convent books stated, that the <i>Time of Judgement</i> has passed and was not the end of the world, but if that was a good thing is arguably. I personally, wish for the 20th Anniversary editions to be timeless, and if the present the world in a certain way, it should be a no-brainer to add a sidebar and tell the reader, that something about this aspect of the world is/was/will be different in books from other editions, due to what ever reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it wasn't that the Time of Judgement happened in the new Rev Ed CBs but rather that they exist in a world where the Opening Trinity of the WoN, 6GM and AS happened but the later Rev Ed events that led to the ToJ didn't occur and the world kept turning. But they also point out that those events still <i>could </i>happen, leaving it up to the individual storytellers and players to decide how to incorporate them.<br /> <br /> And its worth noting that this is similar to Brucato's personal canon has the Avatar Storm happening but then receding, doing its damage without totally crippling the possibility of beyond-Earth adventures. Of course that's not the canon of M20 but that is definitely my canon for M20.<br /> <br /> As for Wr20 and Orpheus, my current personal canon is that the 6GM hasn't happened yet while the Orpheus Group exists and has been investigating ghosts openly since 1999, at first solely in the Skinlands but more recently they've begun to 'hire' ghosts and venture into the Shadowlands. Most wraiths have no real clue about Orpheus and their projectors, those that do, especially in the Hierarchy, are of differing opinions. Some believe they should stay away from those meddling Quick, others want to destroy the company and its competitors, others want to reach out to them whether for help or to use them for their own gain, etc. Also Pigment has only recently begun to appear on the streets and a handful of Hues have been created by it but even less wraiths know about this yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T14:16:19-08:00","id":329538,"title":"","content":"*Ripps the caul off this thread*<br /> <br /> If people backed the kickstarter we'd get both in the W20 book. I mean a proper treatment of those Orpheus guys, not a paragraph saying 'yeah, we know they are out there but not enough to say anything'.<br /> <br /> So do your part and bring those Quick-and-Deadies down here, we need all the help we can gt. Yes, I said <i>we.</i> I need you to fight the Hierarchy one way, or the other.<br /> Don't make me come back here with my soulforging buddy and repurpose y'all into weapons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T22:11:41-08:00","id":329881,"title":"","content":"I didn't know you can get Orpheus in Werewolf 20th.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avat